        "prefix_token_count": 64,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Identify the type of probability distribution involved. This scenario follows a binomial distribution because there are two possible outcomes (treasure or no treasure) for each island, and we are interested in the probability of a specific number of successes (finding treasure) out of a fixed number of trials (visiting islands)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 810,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 811,
        "char_start": 340,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 192,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 193,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Use the binomial probability formula to calculate the probability of finding treasure on exactly 4 out of 7 islands. The formula is given by $P(X = k) = \\binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k}$, where $n$ is the total number of trials (islands), $k$ is the number of successes (islands with treasure), $p$ is the probability of success on a single trial, and $\\binom{n}{k}$ is the binomial coefficient representing the number of ways to choose $k$ successes from $n$ trials."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1043,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1044,
        "char_start": 813,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 286,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 287,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Substitute the values into the formula. Here, $n = 7$, $k = 4$, and $p = \\frac{1}{5}$. Therefore, the probability is calculated as:\n\\[ P(X = 4) = \\binom{7}{4} \\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^4 \\left(1 - \\frac{1}{5}\\right)^{7-4} \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1265,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1266,
        "char_start": 1046,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 368,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 369,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Calculate the binomial coefficient $\\binom{7}{4}$. This is the number of ways to choose 4 successes out of 7 trials, which is equal to $\\frac{7!}{4!(7-4)!} = \\frac{7 \\times 6 \\times 5}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = 35$."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1556,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1557,
        "char_start": 1268,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 506,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 507,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Substitute the binomial coefficient and simplify the expression:\n\\[ P(X = 4) = 35 \\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^4 \\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)^3 \\]\n\\[ P(X = 4) = 35 \\times \\frac{1}{625} \\times \\frac{64}{125} \\]\n\\[ P(X = 4) = 35 \\times \\frac{64}{78125} \\]\n\\[ P(X = 4) = \\frac{2240}{78125} \\]"
      }
    ]
